{Sentence 1: "What is Color Gamut?"}
{Sentence 2: "It is defined as the range of colors which a particular device can produce or record."}
{Sentence 3: "It is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram."}
{Sentence 4: "For example, the primary colors of monitors are red, green, and blue."}
{Sentence 5: "Hence, the color gamut of a monitor is shown in a triangular area enclosed by the color coordinates of the monitor's red, green, and blue colors."}

{Color gamut is defined as the range of colors which a particular device can produce or record.}
{It is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram.}
{For example, the primary colors of monitors are red, green, and blue.}
{Hence, the color gamut of a monitor is shown in a triangular area enclosed by the color coordinates of the monitor's red, green, and blue colors.}
{A chromaticity diagram with different color gamuts is shown in Figure 1.}

{Sentence 1: "The color gamut of a monitor is shown in a triangular area enclosed by the color coordinates of the monitor's red, green, and blue colors."}
{Sentence 2: "The color gamut of a device is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram."}
{Sentence 3: "The color gamut of sRGB is the standard color gamut established by the IEC in 1999."}
{Sentence 4: "The area ratio of sRGB to NTSC is 0.72 to 1."}
{Sentence 5: "The color gamut of AdobeRGB is meant for use in graphic design, mainly for printing purposes."}
{Sentence 6: "DCI-P3 is mainly used in digital cinema, and EBU is used by the European broadcasting industry."}
{Sentence 7: "Rec. 2020 is a newly developed standard for all devices in the future, and it represents almost all the colors humans can perceive."}
{Sentence 8: "The selection of color gamut really depends on your workflow and requirements."}
{Sentence 9: "If your output is online albums or shared on Facebook, then it is suggested you edit your photos in the AdobeRGB color gamut to keep the most colors, then convert to sRGB before posting online."}
{Sentence 10: "The latest trend is to move from Rec. 709 to DCI-P3 or Display P3."}
